-- title:
--   Inertia displacements are congruent to the counit at A
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $R =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) be the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $R$ and finite as an $R$-module; let $J$ be an additive commutative group with a distributive action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) = \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{alg}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $M$ be an additive subgroup of $J$. Assume given a bijection $e$ from `WithConv` of the type of $R$-algebra homomorphisms $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto $M$ which carries the convolution product to addition, $e(f \cdot g) = e(f) + e(g)$, and which is Galois-equivariant in the sense that whenever $g(x) = \sigma(f(x))$ for all $x \in H$ one has $e(g) = \sigma \cdot e(f)$ in $J$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, and let $m \in M$ lie in the additive subgroup of $J$ generated by the displacements $\sigma \cdot y - y$ with $y \in M$ and $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Then the point $e^{-1}(m) : H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfies $A.\mathrm{valuation}\bigl(e^{-1}(m)(h) - \varepsilon(h)\bigr) < 1$ for every $h \in H$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit of $H$, its values being taken in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ through the structure map of $R$.
--
--   This is the pointwise form of the assertion that a point of a finite flat group scheme over $R$ obtained from inertia displacements at a place above $p$ lies in the connected component at that place: its coordinates agree with those of the identity section modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. It feeds into [`GaloisRepAdic.iSup_map_levelAction_sub_id_inf_eq_of_finiteFlat_level`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.iSup_map_levelAction_sub_id_inf_eq_of_finiteFlat_level), the finite-flat input used in passing from flatness to ordinarity for the deformation problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRep_valuation_sub_counit_lt_one_of_mem_closure_inertia_displacement.lean

import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_Flat

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
